It would seem likely. The 533 MHz 21164PC is priced at $495 in lots of
1000. OEM-quantity prices for the motherboard are estimated at around
$250.

>By the way, how do the 21164a and the 21164PC differ?

   -No on-chip L2 cache.
   -Small (apparently) performance sacrifice:

    CPU:     21164PC 533MHz    21164 500MHz 8MB L3   21164 500MHz 2MB L3

   SPECint95:    14 (est.)         15                 14.9
   SPECfp95:     17 (est.)         20.4               16

     (For the 21164PC SPEC estimates, it's not clear how much off-chip
      L2 cache at what cache speed was assumed.)

   -It has Digital's flavor of multimedia extensions (as will the 21264) 

   -Cheaper. Much, much cheaper.
    Currently a 500 MHz 21164a goes for $1450 in 1000-unit quantities. 
    That makes the 533 MHz 21164PC almost $1K less expensive at $495.

   -It looks as though the AlphaPC 164SX motherboard will have much improved
    memory speed over the older 164PC motherboard.

