>Can install an external floppy drive to the slave printer port on a
>VT200 to save a file.

Is that a question, or a statement?  If it's a statement, I think
it's wrong.

> Will it save to the floppy in ASCII or what.

I can't think of any way to connect a floppy drive directly to a
printer port and get it to save *anything*.  At best, you might
be able to erase the first track of an already formatted disk.

I think you probably would be best off by using a PC-clone as a
terminal emulator and capturing the data you want to a file.  I
highly recommend MS-DOS Kermit or Kermit 95 for this application.
See http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ for more details.

