Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



This is a followup to my enquiry a couple of weeks ago about running
Digital Unix on a Multia. Thanks to all those who sent helpful advice -
unfortunately all of the related articles have expired here now, so I
can't easily refer to them directly, but here is the summary.

First, a Digital Unix license for a PCI-33 system (QL-MT4AE-6Q) is several
hundred dollars less than one for an Alphastation, and is even the correct type
of license for the specific machine. I couldn't find anyone at 800-DIGITAL who
could tell me that, so many thanks to Alastair Martin for the information.

Second, I was asking about obtaining higher TGA resolution than 1024x768
when running unix. The web site http://www.annex.co.uk/systems/udb.html
actually has a useful picture of the SRM resolution jumpers (which are
unlabelled in real life). Changing those does actually seem to affect the
SRM resolution, but unfortunately, X still starts up at 1024x768.

Incidentally, the useful Multia service manual EK-MULTS-IN is available online
at http://www.brouhaha.com/~eric/computers/udb.html

I have also tried adding a file /var/dt/config/Xservers containing
the line:
   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen0 1280 -vsync 72

-which seems to work ok for an Alphastation with 3D10 graphics card, but
no effect on the Multia. Strange, as the TGA card is certainly capable of
more. I don't know if there's anything else I could try...

Graham



