Gene Hightower  <gene@yap.organicus.com> wrote:
>So I've got the thing at the ROM prompt -- what now?  Tried a few
>obvious things (like what works on a VAX or a Sun) with no luck.
>
>Anyone remember anything about this beast?  It's a MIPS based systems
>from the early 90's.

at the chevron, do a printenv to see the environment for the monitor. 
One of them is called bootmode or boot_mode, i dont rmember how it is spelled
but its not easy to confuse. 
It is presently set to a, i would expect. Change it with the setenv 
command to a *. 

If youlike you can clear the bootpath variable but it isnt important.

next boo tthe system manually by specifying a path- 
boot rz(0,0,0)vmunix, for example, will boot vmunix from
controller 0, device 0, partition 0. 
(you can also use DEC's partition letters, as in boot(0,0,a)fancykernelname 
if you like)

now the system will stop halfway through the boot process and wait at a
single user prompt. Exiting the single user shell will allow the boot
process to continue and bring the system up multiuser. 

On my vax, which runs ultrix 3.0, if you hit ^c quickly while it is booting up
you can cancel the autoboot and it will come up single user, 
but i cant recall for sure if this worked on my decstation as well. 
my guess is that it would, but you never know ;)


happy hacking,
isildur



