Gene Hightower (gene@yap.organicus.com) wrote:
: So I've got the thing at the ROM prompt -- what now?  Tried a few
: obvious things (like what works on a VAX or a Sun) with no luck.

You should be able to do the following

>> boot #/path

where # is the slot number of the device you are booting from and path
is the file specification of the program.  If you wanted multiuser
mode you would use the -a option.

For example

>> boot 3/rz1/vmunix 

would boot from drive rz1 in slot 3.

I claim no credit for this.  I actually have an old 5000 manual.

