In article <w4k67yfygr4.fsf@pine.comlab>, Jonathan Hill <jonh@pine.comlab> writes:

:	I'm having some problems on an Alpha 8400 with memory
:consistency between processors. I've developed some barrier
:synchronisation routines...

  There are Alpha PALcode and hardware instructions designed and intended
  for this particular purpose, and -- depending on the operating system in
  use -- there are various other routines layered on these primitives.

  See the LDx_L and STx_C locked-load and locked-store instructions, and
  see the MB and WMB instructions, and see the IMB PALcode call.  (There
  are other PALcode calls that may be of interest, and particularly some
  of the interlocked PALcode calls present in the SRM PALcode...)

  One of the chapters of the Alpha Architecture Reference Manual (AARM)
  covers cache coherency, and mentions multiprocessor memory management
  machinations.

  If you're working at this level, you need a copy of the AARM...

