>Just what is DECnet?
>
>Is a datagram protocol, like IP and IPX, that can run on top of
>Ethernet? Or is it a hardware protocol like Ethernet? (I've heard it
>described as a "intentionally non-compatible breakage of Ethernet").

DECnet can be run over
asynchronous or synchronous serial lines.  So DECnet doesn't
necessarily have anything to do with Ethernet.  A DECnet link
can certainly exist (even coexisting with other protocols) through
an Ethernet connection, of course.

