phoenix (phoenix@hn.planet.gen.nz) wrote:
: I have a Vaxstation 2000 running Ultrix 4.3 with Decwin.
: for some unknown reason it will not make it into multiuser mode.
: If Xqvsm (its mono) is run at the end of /etc/rc as normally configured
: it just sits at the Xwin blank init screen. All you can do is move the
: mouse about.
: if i hash out the Xqvsm line in /etc/rc it starts in single user mode at
: a crash prompt. Replacing the Xserver with /bin/login has no effect.
: Also none of the services called during either /etc/rc or /etc/rc.local
: seem to start as ps reports only about 4 processes - probably something
: to do with arriving at the crash prompt.

You don't run Xqvsm out of /etc/rc.local.  You instead put a line at
the bottom of /etc/ttys to enable the console on the graphics adaptor.

:0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter -C /usr/bin/dxsession -e" none on
secure window="/usr/bin/Xqvsm -su"

Be sure to turn off the serial tty console at the top of /etc/ttys.

After editing /etc/ttys, either reboot or do: kill -HUP 1

Barry Kort



