In article <5gqesj$l0u@crinos.stanford.edu>, jimge@crinos.stanford.edu (Jim Geist) writes:

:Does anyone know the pinout for the DB-9 serial console connector on
:the back of a VAXStation? It's most definitely *not* the same as the
:current DB-9 standard... 

  The pinout was an older RS-mumble standard which a company that
  shall remain nameless chose not to follow...  (I don't remember
  which older RS-mumble, now EIA-mumble, standard it is, however.
  It looks like the first few pins from EIA-232-x...)

  I'd order an H8575-B adapter and some BC16E cabling, and use MMJ...

  However, here is the MicroVAX DB9 pinout:
  
	1 - Protective Ground
	2 - Transmit data
	3 - Receive data
	5 - Data Terminal Ready
	6 - Data Set Ready
	7 - Signal Ground

  Pins 4, 8, and 9 can/do have implementation-specific behaviour.

