Hello:

Local> SHOW SERVICES

will show all LAT services that the DECServer has received an announcement for.
If the said system is not currently up (LAT protocol), it will show a status of
unavailable and if you do a 

Local> CONNECT servicename

the connection will timeout and the service will disappear from the list. The
CONNECT can be shortened to C. 

NOTE: This server will only do LAT protocol. Make sure there is a
@SYS$STARTUP:LAT$SYSTARTUP.COM or @SYS$STARTUP:LTLOAD.COM (for older VMS's)
somewhere in the SYS$STARTUP:SYSTARTUPx.COM file 
where x=	nothing for VMS4.x (?)
		_V5 	for VMS5.x
		_VMS 	for VMS v6.x
		???	for VMS v7.x

You could also run this from the command line to test if it runs correctly.

Good luck.
Steven Underwood

