I don't know your model of Starion at all, but chances are a 16MB
parity SIMM, 70 ns. or faster will fill the bill.

The best you might be able to do is draw an inference about the memory
speed by running Ray Van Tassel's CACHECHK utility or QuarterDeck's
Manifest, both of which do some memory speed benchmarks.

Better still, open up the case and examine the memory chips or SIMMs
already inside.  If the chip part numbers have a -70 or -7 suffix,
they are 70 ns.  -60 or -6 is 60 ns... Ben Myers

