Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <5gj3cd$idk@zam201.zam.kfa-juelich.de> a.arnold@kfa-juelich.de writes:
>
>On an AlphaStation running Digital Unix, is there a way for a C program to find
>out the processor's clock speed?  

#include <c_asm.h>

main()
{
     unsigned int start, finish, count = 0;
     start = asm("rpcc %v0");
     count -= start;
     sleep(1);
     finish = asm("rpcc %v0");
     count += finish + 500000;
     count /= 1000000;
     printf("CPU is %d Mhz\n", (int) count);
}

