> NFS' first order problem is not performance, scalability, cache
> coherency, or even global namespace. Bit by bit those issues have
> either been solved or have become non-issues. The first oder problem
> for NFS is security. Not so much that there isn't security ...
> security schemes based on Diffie-Hellman and Kerberos V4 have been
> around for NFS for years. The problem is that the security schemes
> aren't generally available across all NFS implementations.  NFS V4 will
> fix this by making it a requirement to support a minimal set of common
> security mechanisms before one can claim conformance to the NFS V4
> protocol.

As a Certified Security Fanatic, I have often referred to NFS as
"No File Security", but as with any other "checklist" capability
it is important to understand one's true application needs.

I currently have an application where NFS works just fine between
vendors because security is handled at another level.

Larry Kilgallen



