If you do need to convert binary file formats, you will need to know the
precise file format. Provided this is available, the simplest converter
you can lay your hands on is the Perl 5.003 interpreter, which is public
domain and available for a wide variety of operating systems. The 'unpack'
function will extract bit and byte fields in any format (it's a bit like
sscanf in C, but for packed binary).

