Mark, there are some lower cost options that you might 
want to look into.  

First, the price you were quoted for the Developers Toolkit
(includes the C compiler, debuggers, etc.) was the "Standard"
price including 1 year of rights to new versions.  That price
can be reduced to $1,798 if you ask for "List".  Further,
this product is offered with a choice of licenses: Traditional
allows unlimited use on the system; Concurrent use allows one
use at a time.  The list price for a Concurrent license is
$1,121.  

I don't know much about Open3d and version compatibility with
Digital UNIX, or whether you even need it.  You can do some 
research by looking through Software Product Descriptions on 
Digital's web page http://www.digital.com/info/SPD/ 
In addition to Open3D, you may also want to look into 
"Multimedia Services" runtime which I think provides the 
support for the FullVideo card.  If you do need to order
Open3D, you should be able to order an Open3D only kit for 
$225 rather than the full layered product software library
set that was quoted at $1,043.

You probably want to give some thought to whether you want 
to upgrade MATLAB and Digital UNIX, or whether you want to
stay on Digital UNIX V3.2 (but upgrade to a later V3.2 release).
You should be able to order a kit for Digital UNIX V3.2g by
specifically requesting that version.  When upgrading within
the version 3.2 releases, you will not need to purchase a 
new version license, so your cost would only be the $395
for the software kit.  You really need to consider the features
of UNIX V4.0, and the new MATLAB versus the added cost
of upgrading.

