It's more than just the heat.  At higher clock frequencies, the signals
begin to radiate and affect other signal paths.  The clocks of some of
the new chips (Alphas are now sporting 300+MHz clocks) are in the UHF
broadcast  bands!  It's hard to keep those signals going where you want
them to.  Capacitance and inductancs also distort the waveforms.  Light
does not suffer from any of this, although reflectance in the
distribution media can distort those waveforms too.

