Peter,

> I'm using an DEC Multia Alpha 233, but in the last time the system
> shows some odd behavior. If the machine runes for a short time it
> comes up with memory errors and stops working. I already tried if
> exchanging the memory modules and cache module helps, no change in
> the behavior. Today I called my local Digital Service Center and
> mentioned the problems I have. They told me that they probably have
> to change the system board and this would cost around 1400$ because
> the system is out of warranty.

The motherboard you need is 70-32588-03 - check with your local
service store what the *EXCHANGE* cost is, this should be somewhat
less than the price for a new MLB, emphasis should be placed on the
fact that you do *NOT* need a new 21066A CPU.

> Is there any other way to get the system (cheaper) repaired?
> (the same system sell in the moment for ~$1000, and I'm don't want to
> throw my machine out)

To be honest it may work out cheaper to pick up a VX41 or VX42 system
(both systems have the same MLB) even second user to fix up your system.
My advice is to try re-seating the cache stick once again, this seems to
resolve the majority of similar problems I have seen.

