In article <332d277e.236986064@firewall.unidec.co.uk>, gary@unidec.co.uk (Gary
Whitehead) writes...

>On 16 Mar 1997 08:51:07 GMT, bliles@power.digex.net (Bryan Liles)
>wrote:

>>I have a couple of axpci33 boards that don't boot.  I have mounted them in a 
>>case, but I can't get any devices to boot.  

>>The board has power and memory.  when I give power to the boards, nothing 
>>happens.  The fan starts, and the keyboard has power, but I get no 
>>video output.

>When we get these boards new, they are configured to talk via the
>serial ports. You might need to attach a terminal to one of the serial
>ports and do something like:

>set console graphics

>to get the thing to boot up via the graphics card

	WHICH AXPpci 33?

	AXPpci 33 comes in two flavo(u)rs:
		SRM console for Unix
		ARC console for Windows NT.

	The Set Console Graphics command applies to the UNIX/SRM version.

	The SRM console will try to be helpful, in that if it does not
	see a graphics keyboard, or a graphics card, it will 'fall over'
	to serial mode.  The 'fall over' is temporary, until a 'set console ...'
	command is issued.

	In serial mode it routes console IO to the COMA port at 9600/1/n.

	(The ARC console sort of does the same thing, but its not real easy
	to use the ARC console in serial mode....)

