  re: OpenVMS 10K delta-time limit: additional info & tools now available

  The OpenVMS operating system has a documented delta-time limit of 10,000
  days (10Kdays), and this limit may result in application run-time errors,
  and in certain OpenVMS components and shareable images, beginning on or
  near 19-MAY-1997.

  A Customer Letter on this topic has been mailed to OpenVMS customers.

  A copy of the Customer Letter, an updated Questions and Answers (Q&A)
  `10K FAQ', and a program to test for the application of the 10K patch
  have been posted at DIGITAL's www.openvms.digital.com website.  (See
  below for pointers.)

  Patch kits are available for OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 through V7.0, and are (or
  shortly will be) available for OpenVMS VAX V5.5 through V7.0.  Patches are
  not needed for V7.1 and later.  See the 10K Q&A for further information on
  OpenVMS VAX prior to V5.5, and on OpenVMS Alpha prior to V6.1.

  Patch kits are available at DIGITAL's web site, and from DIGITAL's customer
  support center: ALPLIBR05_070, and VAXLIBR05_070.

  [The Q&A referenced below incorporates much of the feedback DIGITAL has
  received since the first version of the Q&A was made available; the Q&A
  below is an update to the version I recently posted to the newsgroups.]

    Customer Letter:
      http://www.openvms.digital.com/openvms/letter.html
    Q&A:
      http://www.openvms.digital.com/openvms/delta_qa.html
    Tool to check for patch:
      http://www.openvms.digital.com/openvms/show10K.com
    Current OpenVMS Alpha Patch:
      http://www.service.digital.com:80 -
              All_Databases&query_string=ALPLIBR05_070
    Current OpenVMS VAX Patch:
      http://www.service.digital.com:80 -
              All_Databases&query_string=VAXLIBR05_070

