>
>I have a decstation 3100, 24mb of ram, color frame buffer, keyboard,
>mouse, 19" monitor, and somethings wrong someplace. The diagnostic leds
>are probably trying to tell me something, but since I don't have any
>manuals for it, I don't know what. When I power it up or hit reset, they
>all come on, then they go off, then it starts testing (or I assume its
>testing) and eventually they're all on except for #7, like this:
>
>7 6 5 4  3 2 1 0
>  X X X  X X X X 
>
>Anybody know what this means?

Transcribed from the relevant manual, more or less...

    Self Test Failures

	When a DECstation 3100 is powered on it performs a number
	of self tests.  The normal completion of these tests looks
	something like:

		KN01 V6.71

		7..6..5..4..3..2..1..0

		16Mb..........0

		KN01 V6.71
		08-00-2b-0d-f7-6a
		0x01000000
		>>

	If a test fails, the last number displayed is that of the
	test that failed.  The message "FAILURE - RESET TO CONTINUE"
	may also be displayed.  The individual self test failures
	are:

	Test Code	Component		Action to take
	------------------------------------------------------------
	7		Video SIM module	Contact your service
						representative.

	6		VDAC and PCC		Contact your service
						representative.

	5		DZ serial line		Contact your service
						representative.

	4		System module		Contact your service
						representative.

	3		Keyboard & mouse	Ensure both the keyboard
						and mouse are connected.
						For DECsystems, ensure
						the mouse loopback is in
						place.

	2		Network Interface	The most common reason for
						this failure, is that the
						active interface connector
						isn't terminated.

	1		SCSI bus		If no external devices are
						connected, ensure the
						external terminator is
						in place.  With external
						devices, ensure all the
						connections are secure and
						and the bus is correctly
						terminated.

	0		End of test		Nothing to fix...

    Interpreting LED self-test codes.

	LED Display	
	1 = LED on
	0 = LED off	Hex Code	Component
	-------------------------------------------------
	0111 1111	7f		System Module
	1011 1111	bf		Disk/SCSI
	1101 1111	df		Keyboard
	1110 1111	ef		Memory
	1111 0111	f7		Mouse
	1111 1111	ff		LEDs set at power
					up or reset.

>thanks,

You're welcome.

>Andrew Kieschnick

