It comes with the Language Reference Manual (BIG!) and a "Getting Started"
manual in hardcopy - the rest is on the kit (the documentation is installed on
your hard disk by default.)  The Info Viewer in DevStudio makes looking up
things very easy - you can highlight a keyword in a program, click on a Search
button, and it will show you the appropriate manual pages.  You can also
install it such that the documentation is not copied from the CDROM,
requiring that you insert the CD to read the manuals.

The LRM is based on the one we've been shipping with our other Fortran
compilers, expanded to include the new features and with information for
all our platforms, appropriately "coded" to make it easy to see what features
are on what platform (most are on all...)

The manuals that are on the CD are available that way only.
