These are good points... Actually, the reason for having the 
real/imaginary separated like that goes back to when I had 
those routines coded in  assembly level routines on the CM5. 
I could go into details if you like,  but I could get better 
performance that way. As for the two calls to D_slash...
yes, that takes the part of the matrix-vector multiplication of
conjugate gradient, and I don't know whether I would call it
a linear operation or not. I guess I would.

> 
> > The "matrix" that is inverted is not really a matrix, ok? So your
