> OK, while I still don't understand the physics involved, then don't
> call this function matrix_matrix_multiply when it is in fact something
> completely different.

It IS a matrix-matrix multiplication! It multiplies two SU(3) matrices
(SU(3) matrices are special (det = 1) unitary complex 3x3 matrices).
Seriously, I do know what I am talking about. Imagine you spent a
couple of years working on an algorithm, and someone told you that you
had accidently used a cross-product calculation instead of a 
matrix multiplication.... heh. I think you may be confused as 
to what the "matrix" is. The "matrix" used in the CG routine does not
have seperate real and imaginary parts.... but its elements are
SU(3) matrices which do.

