:) Robert Harley is not a physicist (although he is very smart, and
may be a mathematician, I think), and he rewrote several routines
(in fast_routines.c, the very ones you are probably using). His
changes improved the performance on RISC CPUs substantially, so it is
entirely possible to optimize and improve this code without knowing
any QCD.

How about you rewrite a couple of routines, and make them look pretty?
