I am having a problem with the parallel printer port on a
AlphaStation 200 4/166.   It works perfectly when connected
directly to one printer (an old Toshiba P1351), but hangs
when connected to another (an AST/Camintonn TurboLaser).   The
TurboLaser works perfectly when connected to an ordinary PC.

I then tried using a printer sharing switch (Linksys DCAS221)
to allow both the PC and the Alpha to share the Toshiba printer.
The PC can print perfectly, but the Alpha hangs.

I swapped the input port connections on the Linksys switch, but
the Alpha could still not print.   I swapped the cables, but still
no joy.   I then connected the cable from the Alpha directly
to the Toshiba printer, and it started printing immediately.

It would appear that something about the Alpha's printer port
is super-sensitive to what it is connected to.   Out of two
printers and one sharing switch, it works with only one printer.

Has anyone else experienced similar problems?   Does anyone have
any suggestions for solving this?

Is there a DEC support organization that could help solve this?
I am afraid that DEC would simply say, "It works with one printer,
so that proves there is nothing wrong with the Alpha.   All your
other equipment must be bad."

