|>a DEC CDROM ?
|>

I think you need to be able to set the CDROM to 2048 byte blocks (or maybe thats
512 bytes - whichever PCs do not normally use). But that may be incorrect info
(and even if it used to be correct, things may have changed). Try it and see,
you (probably) won't do any harm.


