Alpha was designed to have up to a 25-year lifetime, with a
1000x speedup (including multiple processor support) over
that time. It's going to be around for a while.

> And joking aside, is there really any point in more than 64bit
> addressing?  What would you do with 128bits of addressing?  Memory map
> all hosts on the internet? 2^64 ~= 16e18, suffices for a hundred million hosts
> at 160 000 Mb virtual memory each.  Guess 64 bits is still enough for a
