I expect the benefits would come with the 128-bit data bus, rather
than the 128-bit address space. Remember, the assumed idea was to 
use the chip for a specialized purpose - image processing - which gets 
benefit out of being able to work with 128-wide data on the chip.

As for a 128-bit address space... you're right, it will be a
while before anyone needs a 40 million trillion trillion 
megabyte VM space - 64 bits should last a while :)

