Chris Ruemmler wrote:

> It would be interesting if someone posted results for a IBM Power 2
> (or Super Power 2), I imagine these might get even better results than
> the PA-8000 in terms of efficiency, even though they have slower
> clocks (77Mhz and 135Mhz).

I can't comment on this particular code, but a few months back
we benchmarked a float-intensive (comp AND memory) fluid
dynamics program (f77) on a 66 MHz POWER2 and a 200 MHz 604e;
the POWER2 ran the code twice as fast as the 604e (and this
was the POWER2 with the "smaller" 128K L1(D) cache) -- i.e.
was 6 times as efficient per MHz.



