>  /PROTECTION=(S:M,O:D,G:R,W:S) /SCHEDULE=(NOSIZE)

I prefer accessing the Appleprinter queues from VMS via MSA directly and not
via DCPS. To my experiencce this more stable, e.g.

Printer queue PRT08, idle, on MPI4::"Printer PRT08@LocalTalk Solte", mounted
 form PS_PLAIN (stock=PLAIN_PAPER)
  /BASE_PRIORITY=1 /DEFAULT=(FEED,FORM=LTR_12 (stock=PLAIN_PAPER))
  /LIBRARY=MSAP$DEVCTL /OWNER=[SYSTEM] /PROCESSOR=MSAP$SYMBIONT 
  /PROTECTION=(S:M,O:D,G:R,W:S)

>and this is the setup of the MSA printer definition:
>
