Kevin P. Neal wrote:
> 
> "Bill Smathers" <joe.clark@avnet.com> wrote:
> 
> >Very new to Digital UNIX... mostly HP-UX here... what is the backup command
> >used on Digital ?  On hp-ux we use fbackup and im looking for the
> >equivelent..
> 
> The dump + restore commands are the traditional Unix backup suite.
> 
> DU has dump and restore.
> 
> DU also has vdump and vrestore, which are filesystem independent*
> (dump isn't). Use them.

Actually, the main reason to use vdump and vrestore (besides the fact
that dump and restore don't work on ADVFS) is that they have the ability
to record redundant block group information, so that, for example, if
you record one redundant block per each 10 blocks, then if you lose one
block in that group (bad block on tape), then you can still recover the
data.  Of course, losing two blocks in a group will still result in the
loss of data.  I'm amazed that such an obvious feature is not present in
most unix backup software...
