        No, it's $300 (maybe  $350  by  now)  to  transfer _all_ the SIP
    licenses  on the machine (VMS, VAXcluster, DECnet) from the original
    purchaser to you.  We've done this recently (about 5 months ago) for
    a pair of 6420's.  No problem.  E-mail me if you want more details.

        My understanding is that  licenses  for layered products are not
    transferable.   That didn't affect us for a number of reasons  (CSLG
    primarily).

        One problem comes when you talk  to the _license_ people instead
    of  the  license _transfer_ people: the license people look  up  the
    _original_ list purchase price for a system, e.g.,  your  6220,  and
    tell  you THAT is what it costs!  It's really sad, they're so out of
    touch...

