Nico Garcia wrote:
> Hmm. As I understand it, the portability of NT to DEC hardware is due
> to the settlement of the lawsuit between DEC and Microsoft concerning
> the raw amount of code that David Cutler and the other people hired
> away from DEC wrote into NT after DEC cancelled the release of the
> new VMS based operating system they were working on.
> 
> Rather than finish bankrupting Microsoft by hitting them for triple
> damages, based on sales not profits, of every copy of NT they sold,
> they agreed that NT would be ported to every new DEC platform.
> 
> Or, in English: NT works on DEC because it is VMS with a new name....

Catch 1: Windows NT was ported to Alpha years ago, and the non-existent
lawsuit in that rumour only happened last year. An agreement to port
couldn't really be based on a future event.

Catch 2: Windows NT was not ported to the TurboLaser (8200/8400)
systems, and currently has not (officially) been ported: an example that
demonstrates Windows NT was *not* ported to every new Alpha platform.

Catch 3: Windows NT is not VMS with a new name. OpenVMS is VMS with a
new name. 8-)

Catch 4 (since you didn't explicitly mention Alpha): StrongArm is a new
DEC platform, but I haven't seen a Windows NT port for it.
-- 
