In article <E6KI0C.7ws@ifwb.wupper.de>, aw@vax3.wupper.de (Andreas W Wylach) writes:
|>
|>Hi everybody,
|>
|>Question: How easy/How difficult is it, to make out of an VAX6000-400 a
|>VAX6000-500 Model. Besides getting the 500-Model CPU is there any backplane 
|>work to do, I mean something like taking an soldering-iron and 
|>changing wires or so ???
|>

There are two ways of doing this.

The easy way is to add a T2019 XMI module which supplies the +3.3V needed
by the KA65A (and MS65A, LA66A and probably a few other things besides). Stir
in KA65A(s) and swap MS62A(s) with MS65A(s) to suit. If you already have
a T2019, just remove the +3.3V inhibit cable. The limitations are that you
have lost a couple of slots and you can't use battery-backup.

The harder involves a full backplane upgrade, this involves swapping the XMI 
card cage, swapping the power regulator, swapping the XTC and swapping the
Power & Logic gubbins. I've never played with a 6000's innards so any and all of
this procedure may be incorrectly described and/or wrong but you'll need the
appropriate manual anyway so it doesn't matter :-)

So if you go the easy route you just need an extra T2019 module and off
you go.

If you want the full gory details, I'll dig out the numbers of the two manuals
that describe the processes.

