I am still waiting for others to send me their results (hint, hint!)

Are there any pentium [pro] experts out there? We need you, our
dual pentium pro has been edged out slightly by the 333MHz alpha, and
looks silly compared to the 500MHz beast! Have a look at the routine
below, and tell me if you can get it to run faster. We should
try to stick with C code, so that it remains portable. But, hey,
if you would like to throw some inline assembly my way, I won't
complain! You will get credit in this public domain code...
(Any ideas to make this go faster on any other CPU would also
be greatly appreciated, although Rob Harley's version is a good
deal faster on an Alpha)

In the meantime, I will work some more on the NT specific stuff,
to try reduce some of the overhead. On a 6^4 lattice, using dual
CPUs makes an almost 100% improvement in speed, but not so 
for the 8^4 case.

Anyone have a dual 500MHz Alpha running NT?? heh...

void calc_UdagV(const float *src_U, const float *src_V, float *dest_V)
{
  int index;

  for (index=0; index<sl_node_vol; index++)
  {
    dest_V[0] = src_U[3*0+0]*src_V[0] + src_U[3*0+0+9]*src_V[0+3]+
                src_U[3*1+0]*src_V[1] + src_U[3*1+0+9]*src_V[1+3]+
                src_U[3*2+0]*src_V[2] + src_U[3*2+0+9]*src_V[2+3];

    dest_V[1] = src_U[3*0+1]*src_V[0] + src_U[3*0+1+9]*src_V[0+3]+
                src_U[3*1+1]*src_V[1] + src_U[3*1+1+9]*src_V[1+3]+
                src_U[3*2+1]*src_V[2] + src_U[3*2+1+9]*src_V[2+3];

    dest_V[2] = src_U[3*0+2]*src_V[0] + src_U[3*0+2+9]*src_V[0+3]+
                src_U[3*1+2]*src_V[1] + src_U[3*1+2+9]*src_V[1+3]+
                src_U[3*2+2]*src_V[2] + src_U[3*2+2+9]*src_V[2+3];

    dest_V[0+3] = src_U[3*0+0]*src_V[0+3] - src_U[3*0+0+9]*src_V[0]+
                  src_U[3*1+0]*src_V[1+3] - src_U[3*1+0+9]*src_V[1]+
                  src_U[3*2+0]*src_V[2+3] - src_U[3*2+0+9]*src_V[2];

    dest_V[1+3] = src_U[3*0+1]*src_V[0+3] - src_U[3*0+1+9]*src_V[0]+
                  src_U[3*1+1]*src_V[1+3] - src_U[3*1+1+9]*src_V[1]+
                  src_U[3*2+1]*src_V[2+3] - src_U[3*2+1+9]*src_V[2];

    dest_V[2+3] = src_U[3*0+2]*src_V[0+3] - src_U[3*0+2+9]*src_V[0]+
                  src_U[3*1+2]*src_V[1+3] - src_U[3*1+2+9]*src_V[1]+
                  src_U[3*2+2]*src_V[2+3] - src_U[3*2+2+9]*src_V[2];

    src_U += SU3_MATRIX_SIZE; 
    src_V += SU3_VECTOR_SIZE;  
    dest_V += SU3_VECTOR_SIZE;
  }

}

p.s. SU3_MATRIX_SIZE is 18, and SU3_VECTOR_SIZE is 6



