You should be able to plug in the new board and connect the monitor to
the new board and when the system boots, the BIOS automatically detects
that a new video card in plugged in and disables the on-board S3. You
can verify this when the bootup screen comes up; if its displayed on the
monitor and the monitor is connected to the new card, then it works at
that level.

The next step is to install the new video card in Win95. Just follow the
directions with the new card.

Beaware that when the Starion 910 was released we only tested with a
finite number of add-in video cards. Some do not work and some will. The
ones that we've seen that do wirk are the ATI-based cards.

