wade@dax.asub.arknet.edu wrote:
> 
> I have a VAXStation 4000-60.  It had 16MB of ram.  I just added a
> 32Meg expansion.  The startup shows 48MB and a show config at the
> prompt shows 48MB with all the right values in the slots.  (8MB in
> the first 2, 32MB in the second).  After boot, however, VMS still
> shows only 16MB.
> 
> Any idea why this is?

Check the system parameter PHYSICALPAGES. It limits the amount of
physical memory which VMS should use. The parameter should  be set
either to -1 (use all available memory) or to the amount you have (48MB
= 98304 phyiscal pages).

