Lattice QCD with staggered fermions is notoriously 
difficult to get running fast,
because it has a lot of scattering and gathering. I estimate that
about half the time is spent shifting stuff around in memory.
I spent my effort in coming up with an algorithm that minimizes
this "communication". This, afterall, is the key to increased
performance on MPP computers. so, I think the performance numbers
you have given us on your fast alphas are very decent indeed,
for lattice QCD!!

Henley



