>David Evans              (NeXTMail OK)              dfevans@bbcr.uwaterloo.ca
>Computer/Synth Junkie                      http://bbcr.uwaterloo.ca/~dfevans/
>University of Waterloo         "Default is the value selected by the composer
>Ontario, Canada           overridden by your command." - Roland TR-707 Manual

There is indeed a jumper on the M9058.  This particular jumper has an interesting
function.  It is used to disable/enable the RX50 floppy drives.  And yes, RD53's
which are not formatted will appear as though they are offline.  Try changing the
position of the jumper and booting DUA1 or DUA2 (As long as you have an RD53
connected to the M9058.).  Also, make sure that the RD53 is set to DS3 on the 
drive ID jumoer block.
