Hello all,

I called the DEC Service Center to see if they knew the PKUnzip encrypting
key used with the Starion Restore CD (RECOVERY.ZIP).  I have a piggy
Starion 917.  What I wanted to do was selectively restore a couple of
files.  I think it was the first time anyone asked them because they were
clueless regarding the key.

I asked the initially friendly DEC female more and she said, "Why would you
wanna do that?" in a somewhat hostile voice.  I said, "Well, there are
times when I don't want my drive wiped clean (for those of you who don't
know the factory restore process formats your drive before it does anything
else) and yet I still wanna get a couple of these files!"  After a bit of
pleading, I was treated like a "hostile customer" (I wasn't) but it was a
question she couldn't answer and so things went down hill from there. So
much for the guaranteed customer satisfaction message I had to listen to
for fifteen minutes before getting her on the line!  Arg!

I thought she might give me the phone number of their engineering office
but no such luck. I was already persona non grata and anyway, I figure I
can write a "fake" PKUnzip module, to force their software to cough up the
encrypting key(s).  After all, I'm a licensee and I'm entitled to use the
DEC furnished software in the way in which I choose (as long as it's legal
use).  I just thought one of you might already have done this and so I'm
asking if anyone out there in cyberland if you've already got the
encrypting key, please pass it along, I'd be appreciative of the effort
saved.  Thanks,

Jeff





