"Kim, Man Seob" <manseob@samsung.co.kr> writes:

> I have using a NCD X-Terminal connected with Open VMS/AXP.
> The "gold" key mapped to NumLock key is not fuction on the X-Terminal.
> How to change key mapping on DECWindow running on VMS?
> For example, "xmodmap" command is used on X Windows running on UNIX for
> change key mapping.
> What's the command for change key mapping on DECWindow?

xmodmap and xev (which gives you the information needed to use
xmodmap) are both part of the standard VMS DECwindows
distribution. They are in SYS$COMMON:[SYSHLP.EXAMPLES.DECW.UTILS]
along with a number of other basic utilities. These should allow you
to map the NumLock key to KP_F1.
