You can also enable the console (rear panel toggle switch in the 
dot-inside-circle position) and hit Break on the console terminal -- from
there on in, the uVAX will use the terminal as its console, until the
machine is powered down.  Useful if you need to keep the video card 
installed to convince it it's a VAXStation rather than a MicroVAX for
VMS licensing purposes, but a damn nuisance if there really is no prospect
of getting the beast a monitor.  Oh, the box will stall in test A for a
bit while it decides that the keyboard really isn't connected.

