Which RZ28 version do you have. There have been several by different
manufacturers. The quantum version, RZ28-E usually has the pinout on the label
on top. Looking at the front of the drive, from the left, 
	ID1/ID2/ID4/fault light(1pin)/busy light/+5v/spinup/...
this is from memory so be careful, and there are more jumpers to the right that
I don't recall. On the botton of the drive, there are 3 jumpers. The one nearest
the center of the drive is for termination power. The one nearest to the outer
edge is for termination enable. The middle one is not used as I recall.

The RZ28M is a Seagate drive. I don't recall which model.

Good luck

Steve


