Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.admin,comp.os.ms-windows.nt.misc,comp.sys.dec


Hello,

there seems to be a problem while printing PostScript files
from a UNIX system via lpr/lpd to a Windows/NT (3.51, 4.0).
Well, let me discribe once more although this problem has not been 
reported for the first time. Maybe one solution has been found but
not been posted yet.

Client:   
Type: Digital UNIX V3.2D-1 with LPD/LPR (BSD)
Printcap entry is:
lp11|11|HPLJ04|hplj04:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp11err:\
        :lp=:\
        :mx#0:\
        :rm=ppc107.mipool.uni-jena.de:\
        :rp=HPLJ04:\ 
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd11:

Server:
Windows/NT V4.0 Workstation with HP LaserJet 5MP
Print processor: RAW (FF appended)

When one (or a program) can congfigure the lpr qualifiers then
"lpr -l -Plp11 <PostScript-File>" works and the printer compiles
the PS language. But there are a number of UNIX programs that cannot
specify "-l". So i'm looking for a way to specify this flag with
the pritcap entry.             
Second, i tried to modify the temporary files in /var/spool/lp11d with
an
output filter to modify the cf-file (command: "f" ==> "l"), but these
flags
seems to have been passed (to NT) prior filtering.


Well, if anyone has an idea ...
i would be much aprreciated about any hints

With best regards
Uwe Richter

eMail: ur@inf.uni-jena.de



