The person running VMS 4.2 and wanting software would do very well to
take a look over at ftp.decus.org and www.decus.org (two separate
machines!). Or better yet connect with a LUG...so he can find what
has been shared over the years. There is a lot out there of all sorts,
much of it usable on older VMS versions...even with binaries in many
cases. There have been VMS SIG tapes since the spring of 1979 after
all, every 6 months or so. The most recent set were just released, the
Fall 1996 ones. RSX SIG tapes ran from Fall 1977 to about 1992...I regret
I forget exactly when the last one got issues, but there were not many
submissions. There have been pdp11 things on the VMS/L&T tapes lately
when they appear. 

Besides all of which there are a good many separate DECUS library items
at the www.decus.org site. Multiple gigs of material don't however lend
themselves to quick summaries of what there is. Most everything comes
with sources.

