RT11 V4, and a software library named DTLIB.  It is the usual story; I would
like to use some of this hardware for a project, but have minimal
documentation.

The Data Translation Q-bus modules I have are as follows:

DT2768-1                DRV11 equivalent

DT2769			KWV11-C equivalent

DT2782-DI-C             8 channel differential A/D
DT2782-SE               16 channel single ended A/D
DT2782-SE-C             16 channel single ended A/D

DT3382-32DI-G           32 channel differential A/D
DT3382-32DI-PGH-H       32 channel differential A/D

The only modules I have documentation for are the DT3382s.  I spoke with John
Coughlin at Data Translation (they are still in business, but do not do DEC
any longer), and was told that manuals for the DT2768-1 and DT2769 were
available ($50 each), but that was it.  He also said that some of the product
line had been sold to DEC.

Does anyone out there still use this stuff?  I am looking for:
1) a users' guide (or photocopy) for the DT2782
2) additional software libraries (RSXLIB, VMLIB, ACQLIB...)
3) other DT hardware or information

I am also looking for additional sources of analog I/O boards, specifically
dense (e.g. more than eight channels) DAC boards.  Any ideas?

As always, thanks in advance for the help.  I can post a summary of responses
if anyone is interested.

