> KDA50. I don't have them, where to get parts in Europe (i guess used)?

Usually, a KDA50 is installed in a 3500 in the last (leftmost) slots. 
Do all of the Q-bus slots between the KDA50 and the CPU have something
in them?  If not, the interrupt chain is probably broken.  I don't
remember whether or not SHOW DEVICE will find the disks when the
interrupt chain is broken, but it might not.

Also, the channel between the KDA50 and the RA70 must be enabled.  This
is usually done with the A & B select buttons on the front panel.  Is
the cable from the front panel connected to the drive?

Good luck!

