> Trying b dua0 gives device inactive.. Since I am new to Vax is there a 
> way to test the KDA50, other that the ones found in t 9e.

  If your CPU has tests numbered that high, it probably also has some sort
of "show device" and "show bus" commands. It may even respond to "help"
with a useful command list.

  The first MSCP controller should be at address 772150 octal - perhaps yours
is jumpered for some other address.

  Also, there should be some LED's on the KDA50 boardset - posting what they
are doing might be helpful.

