> UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)
> - ?
> I guess DUA0 should show up here?????

  Yes. What sort of drive do you have? Should be RA-something. There is a
heavy black cable from controller to each drive. It doesn't matter which
controller port the cable is connected to. Follow this cable to the drive
and see which drive port it's plugged into (A or B) and make sure the
drive's front panel switches are set to the same port (A or B) as the cable
goes into.

  Also, these cables don't have straight-through pinning - you need an odd
number of cables between the controller and drive. [You can't just take,
for example, an RA90 out of a SA600 and use a single cable to connect it to
the KDA50 - you need another bulkhead and cable to flip the pins around].

