Usually if you are getting a device inactive message, the drive is not
talking to the controller..You are already past the above info. , however a
sho device at the >>>
prompt will tell you if the drive shows up or not..You should be able to
see the lights on the KDA50 change from a "strobe rotation" to a 4 then 5
alternate pattern on the drive control board. If you are getting this, most
likely the KDA50 is ok.
If now drive shows on a show device, check your SDI cables..
If the drive is there, but you are getting "device inactive", this is BAD
news!
This is often the sign of a crashed HDA..the drive, if its an RA8? drive
can help you on fault isolation as well, check on the "personallity board
for a fail code in the leds near the front of the board...Let me know if
you have a fault, I can look 'em up for U.

Good luck..    -Doug-



