If it shows the drive, check the HDA for the heads being locked
(Assuming RA8?).
Also check for the belt being connected properly from the motor
to the bottom of the HDA.

There is a white plastic lever on top of the HDA (Head Disk Assembly)
that is used to lock down the heads for shipping. and a lever on the
inside of the drive box to disconnect the drive belt. You have to
release two screws/bolts/??? hidden in the grill on the front of the drive
to open it up to see the HDA. (Usually hex screws, but it changed
several times over the years). Then the entire front/top of the drive will
open up, and you can get access to the HDA.




