in DECLaser 2100plus Printer Operators Guide, section 6.5 is "Service Call
Messages", it says "Service call messages indicate that the printer
requires servicing by a qualified Digital service representative (see
Chapter 8 for service information).  Service messages are displayed as 
XX SERVICE (where XX equals a number from 50 through 99)."

First, good luck with qualified Digital service representatives, my own
experience was that they are qualified to box and swap, maybe, at best.

Second, the Op Guide suggests trying to power cycle the unit to clear the
fault before calling for service, I would go further and remove and
reinstall the upgrades, with great care.  As I recall, when I installed
the memory upgrade and Postscript cartridge on my 2100plus neither was
particularly easy to get seated properly.  You might want to check the
pins and card guide alignment (for the memory card) for damage or
misalignment.

--bruce mcculley
