Well there it is. I think ours behaves as badly as all yours. DEC have
been quite helpful so far, and replaced the drive a few times, but the
problem always comes back. I Currently have a call open with DEC about this
but I was just told that this DAT loader is not supported under Dunix,
except under Networker which we don't use. I was amazed at this but checked
the Dunix SPD and they are right! (We migrated our drive from a VMS host
a year or so back).

I did discover that when the drive gets into this state it seems to be
related to the tape, and the tape can be recovered by erasing
(with scu mt erase) or writing a tar file on the beginning (usually)
..(I think scu mt erase completes too quickly to actually erase all the tape,
it must just write over the info at the beginning to make it look like a 
blank tape.) Also, I discovered that scu mt erase doesn't work properly on
the TLZ7L, it just hangs after displaying erase, so I have been eraseing
tapes one at a time on our single tape Conner DAT drive.

Of course, I have no guarrantee that this tape erasing really fixes the
problem since its an intermittent problem. I think we've run though about 10
tapes now since we started the erasing without problems. I have my fingers
crossed.

Your situation is very intersting to me since I'm (apparently) running an
unsupported config and therefore don't have a leg to stand on, but you do
run a supported config with the same problem. So, if DEC can fix your
problem there may be hope for me!

Lets keep in touvh on this one.

