marc@ultrix6.cs.csubak.edu (Marc Thomas) writes:

> 
> 
> I can't get a VAX 6500 to load Ultrix 4.4, either from tape or using
> a RIS mop-type load. It seems to kick out becase it can't handle the
> DSSI drive controller on the XMI bus. I also noted that these does
> not seem to be a device driver for the DSSI in /sys/con/vax/GENERIC.
> Does anyone have any ideas or is anyone running Ultrix 4.4 with this
> configuration? Thanks,
> 						Marc Thomas
> 						marc@ultrix6.cs.csubak.edu
> 

Bad luck! It turns out that Ultrix does not support this kind of DSSI
controller. Neither can a VAX 6000 boot Ultrix from a MOP server, a
problem that if I remember correctly is caused by Ultrix requiring
three files (bootblock, ultrixboot and vmunix) whereas VMS only
requires two and that the VAX6000 MOP boot can't handle that.

Is your tape drive also connected to DSSI? We had no problems booting
Ultrix 4.5 from on TK50 tapes on a TK70 connected to a BiBus TK70
controller.

If you have RA disks and RA controllers supported by Ultrix, a
KDB50 or a HSC connected to CI for example you can get your system up
by doing  something similar to what we had to do before we got Ultrix
on tape. This is what we did (it was some time ago so my memory might
be a bit dim):

* Set up a VAX-Ultrix DMS server on a DECsystem 5400.
* Booted an uVAX II equipped with RA controller and one RA90 disk from
  the DMS server.
* Mounted the VAX Ultrix install CD-ROM via NFS on the uVAX.
* Partitioned the RA90 and installed bootblocks with 'chpt'.
* Mounted the 'a' partition of the RA90 on, say, /foo.
* Copied the root file system of the CD-ROM to /foo.
* Mounted the 'g' partition on /foo/usr.
* Ran a 'setld -D /foo <dir>' where <dir> is something like
  /CD-ROM/BASE.
* Created a kernel with the right devices on the uVAX (took about four
  hours due to small memory and an ethernet interface that does not go
  along nicely with Ultrix) and moved it to /foo/vmunix.
* Shut down the system.
* Moved the disk to the VAX6000 and booted from it

This procedure resulted in a system that did not autoconfigure on
first boot but in all other aspects worked fine.

/Erik

